{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "48402975-7c20-8b5b-b9ed-2f860cfc824d",
  "created_at": "2026-02-23T13:06:24-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Donna Cirelli",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Greg Lombardi",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:02:10-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Greg."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:02:13-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, hello. Um, I'm calling about a fence. Whether I need a permit for one. Sorry, I'm on speakerphone, I hope that's okay. It echoes a little because I'm in the bathroom, it's the only room where I get any reception."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:02:29-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine, I can hear you. A little echo, but go ahead. Tell me what you're looking to put up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:02:37-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So it's a short decorative fence, in the front yard. Like, just along the front, by the sidewalk. At 217 Eustis Avenue, up on the Hill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:02:48-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And how tall are you thinking?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:02:52-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Six feet. And I was going to do pressure-treated wood, from the lumber place, the one that used to be the, um, the hardware store on Bellevue. Well, it's not a hardware store now. Anyway, the lumber place."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:03:07-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. Six feet in a front yard is pretty tall for something you're calling short and decorative, just so you know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:03:16-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. Is it? I thought six was the normal number. Like the standard panel size."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:03:22-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So is there a height where it stops needing a permit? Like, under a certain height you're fine, and over it you need one? I don't really get how it works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:03:34-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally, fences do need a permit here, and there are height limits that are different for front yards than for back yards. Front yards are usually held a lot lower. I'm not going to quote you a number off the top of my head, but six feet up front is probably going to be a problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:03:55-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wait, so, sorry. Is the permit the problem, or is the six feet the problem?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:04:01-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both, kind of. You'd need the permit regardless, and the height is something they'd look at when you apply. Two separate things."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:04:10-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Okay, so there's not a height where you just don't need one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:04:16-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not that I'd count on, no. Plan on applying."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:04:20-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. Sorry, one sec, the echo is getting worse, I'm moving closer to the door. [pause] Okay. Also, I rent. Does that matter? Like do I apply or does my landlord?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:04:33-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. If you're renting, you'd want the owner on board, and they'd likely need to sign off on the application. Talk to your landlord first."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:04:44-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And the neighbor. Do I have to tell the neighbor? The house next door, it used to be that, uh, the funeral home. No, wait, that's the other side of the street. Anyway, the neighbor."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:04:58-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I don't think you personally have to go knock on doors as a rule, but the application and the survey show where the property line is, and that's what matters. It's a good idea to give them a heads up anyway. Someone in the office can tell you exactly what the process requires."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:05:18-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So is that a yes or a no? On notifying them?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:05:23-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can't say for sure it's required. I'll put it this way, ask when you pick up the application, and tell them anyway, it saves headaches."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:05:34-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So I get the application where?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:05:38-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Here at City Hall, the inspections counter. Bring a sketch of the yard with where the fence goes and how tall. Do you want me to leave a note with your number in case they have questions?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:05:53-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. It's 401-555-0185."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:05:55-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0185. And your name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:05:58-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Donna Cirelli. C-I-R-E-L-L-I."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:06:00-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, so just to make sure, I talk to my landlord, I need the permit, and six feet is probably too tall in front. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:06:11-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. Landlord, permit, and rethink the height."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:06:15-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks. I'm still a little lost on the height thing but I'll come in."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T13:06:21-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sounds good. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
